    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0243" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1946v01/pg225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB/11–1646</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by John C. Ross, Senior Adviser to the United
                        States Delegation, to the Political Officers</hi><anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d114-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-16"
                            >November 16, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The question of whether there should be any change in the Department’s slates for
                    the elections coming up on Tuesday has been reconsidered in the Department and
                    the decision reached that there should be <hi rendition="#italic">no</hi> change
                    in our present slates.</p>
                <p>It follows, therefore, that all of the political officers and others concerned
                    should campaign actively among the other delegations in support of our slates
                    with particular reference to Belgium for the Security Council.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d114-f1" n="50" type="source" xml:id="d114-f1-content">
                <p>For the names of the thirteen officers who were assigned to the United States
                    Delegation as Political Officers, see footnote 65, <ref target="#pg41">p.
                        41</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
